  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment policies formulated in Iraq, using strengthened LMI systems and LM statistics</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Availability of reliable labour market data and statistics in Iraq remains limited, constraining evidence-based policymaking to address unemployment, underemployment, and labour market transitions. In this context, the ILO has been supporting the Central Statistical Organization (CSO) in Federal Iraq and the Kurdistan Regional Statistics Office (KRSO) in strengthening labour market information systems and labour statistics. Building on the successful implementation of the first national Labour Force Survey in a decade, the intervention will focus on improving labour market data quality, strengthening coordination between institutions, and supporting the establishment of a Labour Market Information System (LMIS) to improve the production and use of labour market data for employment policy development and monitoring.

At the strategic level, the intervention also supports the finalization and implementation of the Iraq Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) 2026&#x2013;2029, developed through consultations with tripartite constituents, UN agencies, and development partners. Aligned with Iraq&#x2019;s National Development Plan, the UNSDCF, and ILO strategic priorities, the DWCP will strengthen policy coherence, national ownership, and results-based implementation through revitalized tripartite governance, monitoring, and evaluation mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
